WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.480
<i>Dearest Mother and Father back home,</i>

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.820
<i>we have reached the end of the rainy season, and the heat continues in earnest.</i>

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.820
<i>I hope this text finds you in good health.</i>

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.450
<i>May I talk a little about a fairy tale?</i>

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.950
<i>Long ago, there lived a giant, a failure of a girl.</i>

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.990
<i>Not only was she a failure, she did nothing to compensate for that failure,</i>

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.080
<i>God, having learned of her actions,</i>

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.990
<i>locked the giant girl up for one week in a room where time flowed differently.</i>

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.420
<i>To her however, it felt like one year.</i>

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.250
<i>This was her punishment, to have to study furiously for her make-up exams.</i>

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.690
Thus, the giant girl was gone for an entire week.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.000
So, for now, please enjoy "Matsurika Holic".

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.730
Shidoh, are you not in?

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.190
Shidoh!

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.520
What is it, Ishima?

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.600
Miss Shidoh is spending a week visiting family.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.920
Dorm mistress.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.950
I came to partake in some of the delicious sweets Shidoh always prepares.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:39.880
I see...

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.910
Her roommate Miyamae is also on a trip.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.200
This will be a lonely week, won't it?

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.380
To think, I can't eat the delectable sweets Shidoh always provides...

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.870
It seems this will be a trying week.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:59.390
Yes. I wish we had a new pastime to help cheer up this gloomy atmosphere!

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.990
Ta-daa! I've thought of a new pastime.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.020
I call it,

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.940
"Learn While You Have Fun: 
Historic Battles - The Dawn of Japan".

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.660
As supplementary teaching materials?

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.700
If you're after the popular "rekijo" niche, wouldn't it be better to go with the Warring States Period?

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.200
Nandaro's...

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.700
What are rekijo?

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.590
They're women who get way too excited

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.710
over military generals and the relations between them during the Warring States Period.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.350
Make note that most of them have no actual interest in the history of Japan beyond that.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.180
I smell money!

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.220
That's right.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.620
The rekijo!

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:38.090
Huh?

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.660
Do it, boy's love! An eyepatch, let's party.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:44.040
They dress up only the catchy parts of Japan's history.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.350
How utterly pitiful!

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:51.520
So, your answer to that lamentable trend is... this?

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.530
I think it's perfect for those who like military commanders and dashing samurai.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:58.660
These figures are often portrayed in novels and TV dramas,

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:01.240
and it would be easy for newcomers to Japanese history to get into, right?

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:06.710
I think it would be good if we could get a lively exchange going on campus,

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:09.170
like, "So, do you favor revering the emperor or expelling the barbarians?"

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.250
It's splendid!

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.840
Shidoh!

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.260
Letting people learn while having fun... It's splendid!

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:23.140
I feel the passion of Miss Kumagai's teaching!

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.400
No, you exaggerate, Shidoh.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.020
That's right. She's just a Japanese history nerd.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:28.850
However...

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.650
I don't think this will convey your feelings to the students appropriately.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:33.400
Huh?

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.860
The make feels cheap. Color copies on thick paper, that's not enough to pique one's interest.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.360
There is a roughness to both texture and usability.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.830
They have these beautiful illustrations on them,

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:47.530
so they should have the same value as collector's items.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.370
But I don't have the budget to make something like that...

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.800
Please, allow me to help.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.170
If I ask the printers at one of our firms, he'll take on the job for cheap.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:03.010
We can bang out 300 starter packs, then we'll follow up with 1,000 five-card booster packs.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:03.890
That many?!

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:08.440
Please wait, Shidoh. Even if you make these, no one will buy them.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:14.060
Please don't worry, Miss Tonomura. The first round at least is sure to sell, I'm sure of it.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:17.470
Rekijo are in right now, but there's no telling when a knockoff will come out.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:20.870
When it comes to card games, the last one on the scene is the loser, so we have to hurry.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.150
If we have them work late, maybe we can have it done by this week.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.570
No, first thing tomorrow morning, we can have them ready to sell!

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:28.540
Once they're finished, let's try selling them at Mihoshi-no-Mori as well.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:32.600
If we can get player feedback, we can make our teaching materials that much more fun.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.710
That makes sense.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.000
We'll sell these, passing them off as supplementary teaching material,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.840
but gradually shape them into a card battle game,

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.670
eventually aiming toward nationwide tournaments.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.410
A strategic move would be to create an appropriate organization,

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.050
like the Japan History Federation or History Link Japan,

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.060
then introduce these as the organization's recommended study aid,

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.180
which should make it easy to get them into bookstores.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:51.480
But having these become more sellable...

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:55.230
We must plug that moat before Miss Kumagai can think clearly!

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:58.210
Should we try making a Heian Period deck next,

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.360
focusing on the popular war of the Genji and Heike clans?

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.430
A Heian deck, fascinating!

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.870
Judging by your reaction, it would seem you already have a concept for it.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:10.120
Naturally, I've already placed an order for the illustrations!

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.670
Leave it to me. I shall spring forth like a mighty arrow!

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:13.410
Ah.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.380
Looks like that arrow has struck Fumi's chest.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:21.420
Incidentally, Shidoh, what brings you to the nurse's office first thing in the morning?

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:22.220
Ah!

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:25.220
I got word from Miss Kumagai.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:29.390
Huh?

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.390
Kanako's on vacation? For a week?

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:36.270
Yes. Mariya said she wanted Miss Kumagai to be informed.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:40.460
Is that so? Kanako certainly has a weak constitution. She often has nosebleeds...

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:44.150
Actually, it's not illness. It has something to do with her family.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:47.580
Yes. And she has make-up exams, too...

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:51.160
Speaking of, it is rather quiet today, isn't it?

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.060
Sure enough, it's lonely without Kanako around.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.940
Indeed. Things are rather dreary.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.000
She was always the center of such commotion.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:02.300
If things are dreary, maybe we should brighten them up.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.920
Oh! Nanami, you're so smart!

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.510
Good! I just happen to have a flower!

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:14.430
I-I just hope this isn't a problem with the PTA!

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:18.950
Momoi, unfortunately, that is not enough to replace the presence she represented.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:22.190
Oh. You can't really tell it's Kanako's desk, now can you?

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.950
So we should do <i>this</i>!

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:26.280
It's perfect, Momoi!

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:30.920
I-I believe that could lead to a misunderstanding!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.370
What do you say we investigate a different approach?

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.870
A different approach?

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.380
That's a wonderful hairpin, Ryuken.

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:47.470
Oh, this? Ayari gave it to me, saying it's not good for my bangs to cover my eyes.

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:51.950
That was made by the student council president, the charismatic designer of Ame-no-Kisaki?

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.220
It's a new item!

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:57.480
How embarrassing. It doesn't suit this rough hairstyle, does it?

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:59.270
Th-That's not true at all!

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:05.280
R-Ryuken, you look wonderful no matter what your hairstyle is!

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:11.410
Thank you. If possible, I, too, would like to have a hairstyle that is popular.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.660
At that moment, no one could have imagined that Ishima Ryuken's throwaway comment

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:21.210
would result in the birth of Ame-no-Kisaki's charismatic up-do hairstylist.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:25.420
I, Tsutsui Honoka, shall make your wish come true!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:31.200
I challenge you!

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:36.060
Two Black Ship cards and Matthew Calbraith Perry, to make the Convention of Kanagawa!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:39.070
Yonakuni, I'm making this a 
"compelled opening of Japan" deck!

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.520
Also, I'm putting Harris on the stage!

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:46.690
Initiate the Treaty of Amity and Commerce!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.570
And now, the trap card!

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:55.750
Sure enough, it was a good idea to hand out a sample to the dorm mistress.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:56.410
Yeah.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:09:01.290
And we predicted she'd force the dorm students to buy them in order to find opponents.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.820
It feels like we're printing money.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.760
Because we incur no costs other than that for printing.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.090
My, this is quite the turnout, isn't it?

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:10.680
Dorm mistress.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:15.020
I'd like to hold the first official tournament this Sunday.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:18.100
Can you finish the booster packs by then?

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:23.350
Yes. Everything is ready to place enough orders to match tomorrow's demands.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:25.850
"Official"? This is bad.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:28.610
There's no way we're losin' the rights to the official tournament here!

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:29.610
Leave it to me.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:35.240
I will undertake the handling of the official tournament to the best of my ability.

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:36.240
Shoot!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.330
"Shoot"?

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:39.830
Oh, no, nothing at all.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:47.380
In that case, I'd like to talk about the winner's prize, penalties, and God's royalties.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:49.630
Royalties, you say?

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:51.630
Oh, yes.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.180
Ayari, it's already dark outside.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:03.230
Yes. But...

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:06.730
Look! It's complete!

00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:12.240
When this big order came in, I didn't know what to do,

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:15.110
but after working at it day after day, it may just work out.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:18.870
I never thought we'd be asked to decorate a desk.

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:23.620
Yes. But I was more surprised to get the thumbs up from the school's side.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:27.750
What's this? Light coming from a classroom, at this hour?

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:34.180
She is the divine goddess, beautiful both inside and out.

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:36.430
How bewitching she appears today, as well!

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:38.700
What is she doing in the second-years' classroom?

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.890
In any case, it's late at night, so should I not see her home?

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:45.110
N-No, this feeling is nothing to regret; it is my duty as a teacher!

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:47.440
I sure was surprised when we came to this classroom.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:51.940
I never thought there'd be flowers and a picture on Miyamae's desk.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:54.470
What's this?!

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.700
I-It's impossible!

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:00.950
Isn't Miyamae on vacation to deal with family matters?

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:04.070
There's only one reason I can fathom

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:06.420
for flowers and a photograph to be placed on her desk...

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:08.540
Born in the morning, dead by night.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:12.210
I know human life is fleeting, but I hope I am mistaken!

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:15.720
Calm down, Touichirou. It isn't certain yet.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:19.010
First, I must find out the truth. 
Then, we move on to the second half!

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:35.920
What pleasant sleep.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:37.930
My own, familiar room...

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:40.090
A mattress just firm enough...

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.810
Gentle birdsong reaching my ears...

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:45.250
What a wonderful morning.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:52.610
Mariya, now that we've returned to the mansion, why not return to your normal appearance?

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:53.530
Don't talk nonsense!

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:55.820
Now is the chance for some overdue fanservice.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:12:01.070
I have to show all my followers out there how cute I am when I'm sleeping.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.990
Don't you think that, with one character gone, this is a chance to make yourself stand out?

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:09.750
That character is coming back tomorrow, huh?

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:13.370
I thought this would be a chance to spend some leisurely time,

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:15.880
but so many things have happened this week, haven't they?

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:16.660
Yeah...

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:21.400
Decoring got popular, up-hairdos got popular, card games got popular...

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:22.750
Yay!

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.760
Sure enough, in terms of story, we don't need that chick.

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:29.190
Shidoh! Shinouji!

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:31.610
Good morning, Father Kanae.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:32.880
Good morning.

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:34.020
G-Good morning.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:38.360
Ah, how divine you appear today as well, my pretties.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:40.570
May we help you with something?

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.200
Ah!

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.910
I-It's about Miyamae.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:44.960
Yes.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.540
She departed the other day.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:47.660
<i>Departed?!</i>

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:51.420
I-I knew Miyamae was no more of this realm.

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:53.040
Yes.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:57.050
She's gone somewhere where she can't be reached, hasn't she?

00:12:57.050 --> 00:13:01.800
Some extra-planar space where the flow of time is different from ours.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:06.060
<i>I knew it! But why was her death not announced?</i>

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:10.430
D-Do you happen to know the reason for her departure?

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:12.190
Well...

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:17.440
I think it was due to the decision to have her do make-up tests for all her subjects.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.070
<i>So she killed herself?!</i>

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:23.700
<i>Life is a burden, but death is as light as a feather. {Brian Sanderson > Robert Jordan}</i>

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.290
<i>Why? </i>Why<i>, Miyamae?!</i>

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:30.680
<i>If you were feeling that lost, why didn't you come to me for counsel?</i>

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:34.710
<i>You did something that foolish over the results of your semester exams?</i>

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:40.180
<i>No. If I think about if for a second, failing </i>all<i> of her exams is strange, isn't it?</i>

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:42.720
<i>If she'd been attending classes, such an outcome would've been inconceivable!</i>

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:47.180
<i>Or did something trouble her such that she couldn't concentrate on her tests?</i>

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:50.930
<i>Or maybe she had something in mind and failed on purpose?!</i>

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:53.390
What is it, Father Kanae?

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.770
Your face seems somewhat troubled.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.280
<i>No! Repairing a shattered vessel is not possible!</i>

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:04.490
<i>What must be considered now is not our absent Miyamae,</i>

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:08.700
<i>but the happiness of the girls before you, Touichirou!</i>

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:14.620
<i>And yet, they are the ones that worry for me when it is </i>my<i> duty to be supportive.</i>

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.940
<i>How pitiful!</i>

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:16.580
Mariya.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:20.770
Father Kanae seems to be regarding us somewhat eerily.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:21.630
Yeah.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.300
Oh, there's the first bell.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:29.200
I'm sorry, homeroom is about to begin. Excuse us.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.140
W-Wait!

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:36.150
<i>Shidoh, Shinouji. How fleeting you seem before me...</i>

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:40.020
<i>Come to think of it, the gaze with which Shidoh eyed me</i>

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.940
<i>was the way one regards a stone by the roadside.</i>

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:47.320
<i>As for Shinouji, she was icy and emotionless!</i>

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.200
<i>Things cannot stand like this!</i>

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:52.160
<i>O Miyamae in Heaven, please watch over me.</i>

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:56.960
<i>I, Kanae Touichirou, will bring forth their true smiles!</i>

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:01.710
<i>Dearest Mama, up in Heaven,</i>

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:06.420
<i>How can I express this situation, difficult to comprehend as it is?</i>

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.610
<i>He who curses others, digs his own grave?</i>

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.720
<i>No. Only "grave" is appropriate in this case.</i>

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.580
<i>The path ahead cannot be read?</i>

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:18.230
<i>Yes. That is close, but it fails to capture my current feelings.</i>

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:20.130
<i>Wait, what is this?</i>

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:21.360
What is this?

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:27.490
Shizu. The trap prepared for Mariya has been sprung.

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:29.600
Huh?

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.240
Father Kanae?!

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.500
How disappointing.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:37.500
<i>You're</i> the one who's disappointing! Dig him out, Rindoh, you idiot!

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:40.500
It would be more environmentally friendly to bury him than to dig out.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:41.590
Idiot!

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:52.220
I'm sorry. Your robes were soiled with mud, so I washed them for you.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:52.880
Hey.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.440
Hurry and apologize, Rindoh!

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:56.210
I'm very sorry.

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:59.560
I never thought someone would be foolish enough to fall for a fake trap.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:04.280
Still, it's a good thing that it <i>was</i> a fake.

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:10.910
Rindoh's "main dish" up ahead consisted of Viet Cong manufactured explosives.

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:15.040
If you'd run into that, there's no telling if you would've emerged unscathed.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:16.290
<i>Ah.</i>

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:21.840
<i>I'd planned to visit Shidoh at home, but I seem to have strayed into a most terrifying place...</i>

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:22.670
<i>But...</i>

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:27.290
Um, you were visiting Mariya at home today?

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.090
Has my little sister caused some trouble?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:35.630
I don't know when Mariya or our parents will be returning, so perhaps I might be of assistance?

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:36.680
<i>They resemble each other!</i>

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:39.520
I-Is something the matter?

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:00.960
Shh! Shut up, Rindoh!

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:05.040
<i>This person's countenance is so charming that one wouldn't think him a man.</i>

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.090
<i>And also...</i>

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:09.720
<i>He has such a lovely fragrance...</i>

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:12.840
<i>No, no, no, no, no, no, no!</i>

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.500
<i>No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!</i>

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:18.270
<i>Calm down, Touichiro! Don't worry, take it easy!</i>

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:21.790
<i>Be calm, Touichiro.</i>

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:24.400
<i>Shizu is Shidoh's older brother.</i>

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:26.860
<i>He is definitely a boy! Boys be ambitious!</i>

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.030
<i>He is definitely a boy! Boys be ambitious!</i>

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:29.790
Father Kanae?

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.570
Is it that difficult to discuss?

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:33.700
Um...

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:36.530
So, I just won't do?

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:40.370
No problem! Be careful!

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.670
Emergency. Emergency.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:43.780
<i>No!</i>

00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:46.950
<i>It's no good. You're heading for eternal damnation, Touichiro.</i>

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:49.800
<i>At this rate, there's no telling what you'll do!</i>

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:52.460
U-Uh, well...

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.550
Murmur murmur, murmur murmur murmur?

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:59.240
<i>If I don't get out of here as soon as possible...</i>

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:00.310
As soon as!

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:02.810
What's this?

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.790
I'm normal! Normal!

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:06.520
Father Kanae!

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:09.820
Did you notice?

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:10.700
Hm?

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:13.760
Father Kanae is not what he seems.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:18.320
He was eyeing you with a gaze not generally given to men.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.740
Don't be silly. You're overthinking things.

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:24.370
No. I simply noticed, nothing more.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:28.750
Kanae Touichirou is a man to be wary of.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.230
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:36.640
<i>I am not her homeroom teacher, 
yet I go to her house unannounced.</i>

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:41.540
<i>Did I not become ecstatic that I was the only one who could console Shidoh</i>

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:43.140
<i>regarding Miyamae's disappearance?</i>

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:48.400
<i>If so, wouldn't this mean that I was indirectly happy over Miyamae's death?</i>

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:53.280
<i>So could earlier have been God's punishment for my lewdness?</i>

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:54.530
Father Kanae?

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:59.480
Shidoh, Shinouji. Are you just now headed home?

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:02.240
Yes. Our club activities ran rather long.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:09.540
<i>Ah, such bewitching smiles. How enchanting you both are, bathed in moonlight.</i>

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:11.710
<i>However...</i>

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.120
Um, by the way, Father—

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:18.470
Excuse me, Shidoh. I have no right to gaze upon you right now.

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:21.220
Huh? Um...

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:28.260
I was going to ask, "Why are you walking away from my house wearing a bathrobe?"

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:34.400
I thought the season for perverted activities had passed.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:42.970
<i>Dearest Mama in Heaven. When I think about it calmly, as a servant of God, love for me is...</i>

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:47.040
Ah! Father Kanae!

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.920
You're the student council vice president?

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:52.090
The night is late. Hurry and go home.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.550
I-I will. I'm sorry!

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:57.720
Huh?

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:03.850
Wh-What's the matter? Why was she so shaken?

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:11.300
But... She smelled so good...

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.040
Right?

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:18.200
Oh. Natsuru, your face looks pale. Are you not feeling well?

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:21.870
No. I'm fine, Ayari. Let's hurry and go home.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:23.700
<i>I-I can't say it.</i>

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:29.960
<i>Father Kanae is a pervert who goes out wandering the campus in a bathrobe...</i>

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:35.340
<i>Dearest Mother and Father back home.</i>

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:39.470
<i>Thus, the seeds of doubt were strewn here and there, and began to sprout.</i>

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:44.140
<i>The week that the giant girl spent away came to a close at last.</i>

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:47.840
Quit lollygagging, Matsurika. We'll be late!

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:55.820
Huh?

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:56.980
Huh?

00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:32.200
Happy Pretty! Sweetie!

00:22:33.750 --> 00:22:37.500
What is it? You are both making strange faces.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.300
How rude. <i>She's</i> the one with the strange face.

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:44.470
The hell is this? My prior offenses haven't been forgiven?!

00:22:44.470 --> 00:22:48.720
Kanako's presence is not required for Matsurika Holic,

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:51.110
so I erased half of her.

00:22:51.110 --> 00:22:54.480
Oh, I get it. Huh? What's Matsurika Holic?

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:59.160
The second half very nearly became Touichirou Holic.

00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:02.320
Which goddamn part was Matsurika Holic?!

00:23:03.530 --> 00:23:07.410
So, you weren't satisfied with Matsurika's Journal and wanted to take over the show?

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:10.950
Ah. It looks like my whole body's about to disappear...

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:13.950
Dearest Mother and Father back home.

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:16.670
Please look forward to the next Matsurika Holic.

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:18.290
I'll be waiting.

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:22.190
Mom, it's me! Me!

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:23.800
Tarou? Is it you, Tarou?

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:25.050
Yeah, it's Tarou!

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:26.590
Ha, gotcha!

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:29.760
My son's name is Fighting Falcon Joe!

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:31.390
You tricked me, bitch!

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:34.890
I never thought you'd name your son 
after an F-16 fighter jet!
